there are many things that batman gets  right about its title character so  what's the deal with that super slow  walk keep watching to find out heads up  spoilers ahead  the caged crusader begins the film as a  terrifying creature of the night  instilling fear into the hearts of  criminals and everyday citizens alike  fear  is a tool however he realizes he needs  to be more than that by the end of the  movie he needs to be a symbol of hope as  much as fear  another aspect the film does  exceptionally well is establishing bruce  wayne as the world's greatest detective  that he's often referred to in the  comics he walks slowly around crime  scenes taking in every detail and when  he receives his first card from riddler  he's able to solve the riddle fairly  quickly he's met his intellectual match  but before he can bring riddler to  justice he'll go through the physical  and emotional ringer to realize what he  needs to become to stop him  it's unlike any other batman film that's  come before and some of the changes to  the character and setting have some fans  scratching their heads one of the most  significant changes involves the speed  at which batman enters a crime scene  many viewers have noted he walks  exceptionally slowly entering a room  this has caused quite a stir on social  media particularly on reddit however  many fans have chimed in with their own  theories as to why this batman is slower  than what we've seen on the big screen  before one reddit user posted a meme  reading batman in this movie walk slowly  when entering crime scenes so that his  lens can record and identify details  with greater clarity one of the newest  gadgets batman sports in the new movie  is a pair of high-tech contact lenses  that record everything the user looks at  it allows bruce to review the footage at  a later time so he can focus on some  more details he and the cops may have  missed the first time around he also  gives the lenses to selena kyle at one  point so that he can look at the  clientele deep within penguins club in  fact the same redditch user made a great  connection stating this is also shown  canonically when he requests selena to  move around a bit slower as he's  tracking everyone's face inside the  lounge of course others suggest the slow  walking goes even deeper a different  reddit user wrote it also makes him seem  even more inhuman and unnatural lends to  his terror hero status both explanations  ring true and it just goes to show the  level of detail director matt reeves  went into crafting a realistic world the  first conversation i had with matt about  it i just knew there was something  radically different from anything we've  seen in my movies before throughout his  existence batman has always sported an  array of gadgets to help him out of a  bind he may not have super powers but he  has plenty of help in other ways in the  batman he has a few familiar gadgets but  there are some new items as well that  assist him when he needs the most  arguably the most important gadget he  has at his disposal outside of the  contact lenses is the liquid he injects  himself with during the final battle  with ridler's henchmen it's never  established what precisely the substance  is some believe it was a mere adrenaline  sharp batman uses whenever he's too  decent and bruised to continue on his  own others think it was a variation of  bane's venom either establishing that  bane already exists in this universe or  that he could potentially come up down  the road one of the reddit users in the  latter category said i'm glad i wasn't  the only one who noticed the serum i  think they're setting up for bane his  reaction to it was very reminiscent of  how bane would react while much of his  gear has been seen in other iterations  of the character the batman adds some  intriguing wrinkles here and there to  make the machines more practical to this  particular version for instance batman  has seemingly always had a grappling gun  but this version springs out of his arm  for quick and easy access  perhaps another reason why batman walks  slowly is due to all the gear he has to  carry around with him check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  movies are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

